WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
today i'm going to be sharing five  things i wish i knew before i started  playing elden ring so let's start with  what is the most important of these by  far and that is that every enemy has a  hidden posture bar which if you deplete  this posture bar you'll open them up to  a critical strike to deal massive damage  if you've played sakurail you'll know  all about breaking an enemy's posture  but the basic idea is that you're  rewarded for maintaining consistent  damage on an enemy light attacks will  prevent the enemy's posture from  restoring fully but you'll need to  employ jumping attacks charged r2  attacks or strong charge spells if you  want to consistently break the posture  of your enemies of course there are  other ways to break their posture as  well such as the new countering system  with shields and also the parrying  system here's the thing a lot of this is  even possible on bosses and yes all the  bosses have this hidden posture bar as  well a couple of minor boss spoilers  coming up so if you want to go in  completely blind go ahead and skip to  this point in the video alright so in  the clip here you can see me staggering  the glenstone dragon using the rock  sling spell which is made more powerful  by the meteorite staff i'm using we'll  touch more on why the meteorite staff  makes it more powerful later in the  video it took three of these spells in  roughly a 15 to 20 second window or so  to consistently break his posture now  because this posture bar is hidden to  the player the only way you'll know how  much damage you need is by experimenting  with different attacks on various  enemies here against bowles the carrion  knight after fighting him a few times i  realized that one charged r2 attack and  two r2 jumping attacks were enough to  stagger him if you do happen to have  these moments and fights where you  aren't able to keep hitting these heavy  attacks don't panic you can keep the  enemies posture bar from fully  recovering by hitting them with light  attacks this is where those smaller  quick items like throwing knives can  really come in handy and of course if  you're close enough you can always throw  in an r1 attack as well moving on to  number two i've actually noticed a lot  of newcomers to from software games or  checking out eldon ring which is awesome  to be honest with you even as a souls  veteran there have been a number of  mechanics i only discovered after  numerous hours of playing the game which  takes us to number two on our list and  that's that you do have the ability to  switch to your offhand weapon while on  horseback this one drove me crazy for a  while guys it seems like such a simple  one that i knew there had to be a way to  do this in the game maybe it even tells  you in the game and i just completely  missed it but if like me you've yet to  figure it out here's how it goes by  default your right hand weapon will be  equipped when you're riding horseback  pressing l1 however doesn't use your  left hand weapon instead it uses your  right hand weapon but swings on the left  side now i'm playing as a mage right now  and i usually like running with my staff  and my left hand and my sword in my  right hand of course you can see the  problem here whenever i hop on my horse  i couldn't figure out a way to switch to  the staff in my left hand but this one's  actually super simple all you have to do  is press the button combination for two  handing your weapon while you're on  horseback so for ps4 ps5 this is going  to be triangle and r1 at the same time  again if you're on horseback rather than  two-handing your right-hand weapon it  will instead switch to your left-hand  weapon now if you're a mage like me and  running the staff in your left hand  what's kind of strange about this setup  is that you will have to use r1 to cast  the spells when you're on horseback  which of course if you were on foot and  holding it in your left hand you'd be  using l1 to cast while you were walking  around normally so that's kind of a  little quirk of the system but it does  still work and it does keep you from  having to put the staff in your right  hand instead alright for our next tip  we're going to stick with torrent here  because did you know there's actually  two ways that you can dismount him of  course the basic way you can set to a  hotkey so you can press triangle on  either one of the directional buttons on  the d-pad or you can even set them to  the quick access menu on the bottom  where you can just press square now the  thing about this system is that it's  kind of slow to dismount especially when  you're in the heat of battle and i just  kept thinking there has to be a way to  leap off torrent while i'm in the middle  of a battle especially if you're wanting  to go from being on horseback to  fighting on foot instead you may think  you just pressed the jump button twice  but no you see torrent has a double jump  ability so if you press your jump button  twice he's just going to simply double  jump but if you're wanting to leap off  him quickly it's actually going to be  the crouch button so l3 for console  players now this can really help out  when you're in the heat of battle and  you need to dismount quickly to try and  engage some enemies on foot rather than  on horseback and even in some boss  fights as well our next tip relates to  the open world as with most from  software games they ask a lot of the  player and put the responsibility on you  to discover things about the game either  through trial and error or carefully  reading item descriptions players can  also help each other through the  messaging system found throughout the  game and honestly early in the game and  even the first several hours of  exploring lim grave you're presented  with a lot of information in a  relatively short amount of time elden  ring is a vast game and when you first  start your map will mostly be blocked  out you probably already know you can  open up more of the map by finding  various map fragments which are  scattered throughout the world they're  always found at one of these little  totems now what you may not know is that  these totems can actually appear on your  map before you've unlocked that area  whenever you find yourself exploring  uncharted territory on your map be sure  to check frequently and see if you have  a little brown icon like this that shows  up and then as soon as you see that icon  pop up on your map you want to go to it  because this icon will show you the  exact position of the totem which of  course has the map fragment with it i  believe when they appear on your map is  tied to either proximity so maybe if you  get close to it or how much you've  explored in an area but i'm not 100 sure  on that one so if any of you out there  know exactly how that happens and when  it shows up leave a comment below to let  me know the fifth thing i wish i knew  before i started elden ring is that some  items have incredibly powerful passive  abilities and you'll only know if you  read each item description carefully now  we already talked about how from  software and eldon ring in particular  expect a lot of their players and this  is an example of that the meteorite  staff i mentioned earlier in the video  actually has a passive ability that  boosts gravity-based sorcery which you  can see here by the way you'll know it's  gravity-based sorcery based on the  purple coloring of both the spell and  its icon also this raptor's black  feathers armor actually includes a  passive ability for a 10 boost in your  jump attacks these are just a couple of  these items there are a bunch of these  items like this throughout the game so  make sure you're always checking those  item descriptions because at first  glance you may think oh this piece of  armor doesn't really look that great but  then you notice it has some incredible  passive ability that might make it  actually worth it for your build if you  guys are curious about my first  playthrough of elden ring i'm posting it  all on my dedicated let's play channel  which you can check out on the right  side of your screen now as always thank  you all so much for watching i'll talk  to you again soon

